Not one is out of place.","hintFor":1,"lateLine":"You almost give up. Then, at the last of the light, there it is."},{"id":"1-2-3","place":"the page about the child","actions":[{"attr":"Intellect","verb":"read the page about the child again"},{"attr":"Craft","verb":"look at how the leaf has worn"}],"clueTitle":"The thumbed leaf","clueText":"The leaf about the child is softer than any other in the book, and dark at the corner where a thumb would hold it. She came back to it often.","hintFor":2,"lateLine":"You almost give up. Then, at the last of the light, there it is."}],"meaningQuestion":"*\"They wept for him before they feared him.\"* What changed between the two?","weekQuestion":"Why are our names on that list?","pull":"**First light. Two hours north. A child was held at that rock, and whatever it is has not finished.**"}'::jsonb),
