rossed"}],"clueTitle":"The notched stick","clueText":"In the gap where he ran, a stick lies dropped, notched down one side. The newest notches are still pale and wet.","hintFor":1,"lateLine":"You go over the same ground twice before you see it."}],"meaningQuestion":"*\"Some locks already know their key.\"* Whose key?","weekQuestion":"Why are our names on that list?","pull":"The morning is getting on, and this is the Widow''s Tooth. Garrick has not gone back to his inn. He is standing in the road with his pack on, looking at the smoke.\n\n**The ruts go that way. So did the man. He will be there before you, and every door will be shut when you come.**"}'::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 1, 4, '{"place":"Fenmark","narrated":false,"tone":"quiet","cupNight":false,"opener":null,"questionTitle":"Why did they take Tamsin, of all the children in Fenmark?","forkA":"She was someone in particular. They came for her.","forkB":"She was the easiest to take.","callback":"The boy says they moved like they''d done it before. The little horse at the rock had sat out a winter or two.","nudge":"{friend:Charm}, of all the children in Fenmark, why her?","nudgeIfLaid":{"piece":"1-4-3","line":"{friend:Charm}, three doors, with children behind them. Why hers?"},"narratedSilence":"Garrick sets a bowl in front of each of you, and for once he says nothing at all.","puzzle":null,"clicks":[],"riddle":null,"leads":[{"id":"1-4-1","place":"the gate at the end of the lane","actions":[{"attr":"Craft","verb":"look at how the gate was left"},{"attr":"Might","verb":"lift the bar and feel its weight"}],"clueTitle":"The leaned bar","clueText":"The gate at the end of the lane is swinging, but its bar has been lifted and leaned neatly against the post, not thrown down.","hintFor":1,"lateLine":"By the time you find it, the fire is the only light left."},{"id":"1-4-2","place":"the one open shutter","actions":[{"attr":"Charm","verb":"stop at the open shutter and wait"},{"attr":"Aim","verb":"look in from across the lane"}],"clueTitle":"The covered cup","clueText":"On the sill of the open shutter stands a cup of milk with a cloth over it. Under the window, a child''s stool is set square to the wall.","hintFor":2,"lateLine":"By the time you find it, the fire is the only light left."},{"id":"1-4-3","place":"the boy, at the gate","actions":[{"attr":"Charm","verb":"ask the boy how they came"},{"attr":"Intellect","verb":"ask the boy what they passed"}],"clueTitle":"Past three doors","clueText":"The boy says they came up the lane in the dark and went past three doors with children behind them.","hintFor":1,"lateLine":"By the time you find it, the fire is the only light left."}],"meaningQuestion":"*\"Marked before the first cry''s through.\"* Marked by whom, and for what?","weekQuestion":"Why are our names on that list?","pull":"It is long past noon when Fenmark lets you go, and the light is already thinning over the fen. Behind you, one by one, the shutters close.\n\n**East. Two hours. He has half a day on you, and he is heading for the only other person alive who has seen that knife.**"}'::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 1, 5, '{"place":"The old charcoal camp","narrated":false,"tone":"wry","cupNight":false,"opener":"Two winters between two children. Some people count in winters. It''s a way of keeping still.","questionTitle":"Is it the same man, twice, or a way of working?","forkA":"It''s the same man, twice.","forkB":"It''s a way of working, not one man.","callback":"The road, the rock, and tonight her shutters. Not one of those men has said a word.","nudge":"{friend:Intellect}, she knows him by a knife, and the knife in that camp is a kitchen blade. Which do you trust?","nudgeIfLaid":null,"narratedSilence":null,"puzzle":{"q":"Has someone tried her house before tonight?","clickText":"The marks on her back shutter are old and new in the same place, and the bar on her door has worn its cleats deep. Someone has tried her house before tonight, and she has barred it every night for a long time."},"clicks":[{"a":"1-5-2","b":"1-5-3","text":"The marks on her back shutter are old and new in the same place, and the bar on her door has worn its cleats deep. Someone has tried her house before tonight, and she has barred it every night for a long time.","solves":true}],"riddle":null,"leads":[{"id":"1-5-1","place":"the woman at the edge of the firelight","actions":[{"attr":"Charm","verb":"sit with her and let her talk"},{"attr":"Intellect","verb":"ask her what she saw two winters back"}],"clueTitle":"The knife, not the face","clueText":"She says she never saw his face, only the knife, and it is the knife she knows him by.","hintFor":1,"lateLine":"It takes you until full dark, but you find it."},{"id":"1-5-2","place":"the shutter he was trying","actions":[{"attr":"Craft","verb":"run a thumb along the marks in the wood"},{"attr":"Intellect","verb":"set the old marks beside the new"}],"clueTitle":"Older marks","clueText":"Under his fresh marks on the shutter are older ones, grey with weather, worked in at the same place, where the bar sits.","hintFor":2,"lateLine":"It takes you until full dark, but you find it."},{"id":"1-5-3","place":"her door","actions":[{"attr":"Craft","verb":"look at how her door is barred"},{"attr":"Aim","verb":"look the door over by the firelight"}],"clueTitle":"The worn bar","clueText":"The bar on her door has worn its cleats deep and pale. She has barred it every night for a long time.","hintFor":1,"lateLine":"It takes you until full dark, but you find it."}],"meaningQuestion":"*\"The power that gives is also the power that takes.\"* What has been given this week, and what has been taken?","weekQuestion":"Why are our names on that list?","pull":"Nobody sleeps much. At first light she walks you to the edge of the camp, and stands on the old charcoal road, grey with frost and ash, and points.\n\n**North. The same man, the same country, the same season. If it comes round like a calendar, the time is now.**"}'::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 1, 6, '{"place":"The Low Ford","narrated":false,"tone":"wry","cupNight":true,"opener":"Six pieces, one map. Eat something before you stare at it.","questionTitle":"Why are our names on that list?","forkA":"We are like the children. They want us too.","forkB":"Meira chose us, to help her find them.","callback":"Meira had this shape on paper before any of you found a piece. Tonight the pieces drew it.","nudge":"{friend:Intellect}, that list has been in your pocket all week. Tell the table what you make of it now.","nudgeIfLaid":null,"narratedSilence":null,"puzzle":{"q":"Why send the cart one way and the child another?","clickText":"One man carried her down to the water, the other went back up to the cart, and the cart went up the far bank at a run, without her. Anyone who followed the cart was following an empty one."},"clicks":[{"a":"1-6-2","b":"1-6-3","text":"One man carried her down to the water, the other went back up to the cart, and the cart went up the far bank at a run, without her. Anyone who followed the cart was following an empty one.","solves":true}],"riddle":null,"leads":[{"id":"1-6-1","place":"the far bank, along the water","actions":[{"attr":"Aim","verb":"scan the far bank from the ford-stone"},{"attr":"Might","verb":"wade the safe line across"}],"clueTitle":"Threads on a thorn","clueText":"On a thorn at the water''s edge of the far bank, a little way along from the ruts, a few woollen threads hang at the height of a child.","hintFor":1,"lateLine":"You almost give up. Then, at the last of the light, there it is."},{"id":"1-6-2","place":"the ruts up the far bank","actions":[{"attr":"Craft","verb":"read the hoofprints beside the ruts"},{"attr":"Might","verb":"cross and walk the ruts up the bank"}],"clueTitle":"Up at a run","clueText":"Beside the ruts, the horse''s prints up the far bank are short, deep and dug in at the toe. It went up at a run.","hintFor":1,"lateLine":"You almost give up. Then, at the last of the light, there it is."},{"id":"1-6-3","place":"the heel-marks at the water","actions":[{"attr":"Agility","verb":"get down to them before the river does"},{"attr":"Intellect","verb":"work out whose feet went where"}],"clueTitle":"A second man","clueText":"Beside the heel-marks, a second man''s prints come down from the cart to the water and go straight back up to it.","hintFor":2,"lateLine":"You almost give up. Then, at the last of the light, there it is."}],"meaningQuestion":"*\"The key that locks.\"* What is locked, and who holds the key?","weekQuestion":"Why are our names on that list?","pull":"**Cross at first light. You will be there by nightfall. Whatever is at the place the map marks, the season for it is now.**"}'::jsonb)
on conflict (series_id, season_number, week, day) do update set data = excluded.data;


-- 2. fire_table: update leaning condition (>= 2 agreeing pins for 'same')
create or replace function public.fire_table(p_party uuid) returns jsonb
language plpgsql security definer set search_path = '' as $$
declare v_week int; v_day int; v_me uuid := auth.uid(); v_data jsonb; v_narrated boolean; v_pieces jsonb;
        v_mine_pin public.fire_pins; v_passed boolean; v_pressed boolean; v_notice jsonb; v_hands jsonb := '[]'::jsonb;
        v_press jsonb; v_prev_w int; v_prev_d int; v_readings jsonb; v_kinds int;
begin
  select o_week, o_day into v_week, v_day from public.my_fire_day(p_party);
  if not exists (select 1 from public.fan_outs where party_id = p_party and user_id = v_me and week = v_week and day = v_day) then
    raise exception 'not at the fire';
  end if;
  v_data := public.campfire_data(p_party, v_week, v_day);
  v_narrated := coalesce((v_data ->> 'narrated')::boolean, false);

  perform public.fire_check_clicks(p_party, v_week, v_day);
  v_pieces := public.fire_pieces(p_party, v_week, v_day);

  -- What is in your hands tonight:
  select exists (select 1 from public.member_days where party_id = p_party and user_id = v_me and week = v_week and day = v_day and (challenge ->> 'pass')::boolean),
         exists (select 1 from public.member_days where party_id = p_party and user_id = v_me and week = v_week and day = v_day and press is not null and not coalesce((press ->> 'left')::boolean, false)),
         (select to_jsonb(s) from public.fire_shares s where s.party_id = p_party and s.week = v_week and s.day = v_day and s.user_id = v_me)
    into v_passed, v_pressed, v_notice;

  if v_notice is null and exists (
    select 1 from public.member_days md
    where md.party_id = p_party and md.user_id = v_me and md.week = v_week and md.day = v_day
      and md.notice is not null and coalesce((md.notice ->> 'pass')::boolean, false)
  ) then
    v_hands := v_hands || jsonb_build_array(jsonb_build_object(
      'kind', 'notice',
      'title', 'What you noticed',
      'attr', public.notice_line_for(p_party, v_week, v_day, v_me) ->> 'attr',
      'text', public.notice_line_for(p_party, v_week, v_day, v_me) ->> 'text'
    ));
  end if;

  if v_passed and not exists (select 1 from public.fire_laid where party_id = p_party and user_id = v_me and week = v_week and day = v_day and kind = 'pass')
     and public.fire_pass_text(p_party, v_week, v_day) is not null then
    v_hands := v_hands || jsonb_build_array(jsonb_build_object(
      'kind', 'pass',
      'title', 'What you heard',
      'text', public.fire_pass_text(p_party, v_week, v_day)
    ));
  end if;

  v_press := public.fire_press_piece(p_party, v_week, v_day);
  if v_pressed and not exists (select 1 from public.fire_laid where party_id = p_party and user_id = v_me and week = v_week and day = v_day and kind = 'press')
     and v_press is not null then
    v_hands := v_hands || jsonb_build_array(jsonb_build_object(
      'kind', 'press',
      'title', v_press ->> 'title',
      'text', v_press ->> 'text'
    ));
  end if;

  select * into v_mine_pin from public.fire_pins where party_id = p_party and user_id = v_me and week = v_week and day = v_day;
  if v_mine_pin.user_id is not null then
    select coalesce(jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object('id', fp.user_id, 'name', m.character_name, 'reading', fp.reading, 'line', fp.line,
        'mine', fp.user_id = v_me,
        'agree', (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(rm.character_name order by r.at), '[]'::jsonb) from public.fire_reactions r
                  join public.party_members rm on rm.party_id = r.party_id and rm.user_id = r.user_id
                  where r.party_id = p_party and r.week = v_week and r.day = v_day and r.target = 'pin:' || fp.user_id and r.kind = 'agree'),
        'doubt', (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(rm.character_name order by r.at), '[]'::jsonb) from public.fire_reactions r
                  join public.party_members rm on rm.party_id = r.party_id and rm.user_id = r.user_id
                  where r.party_id = p_party and r.week = v_week and r.day = v_day and r.target = 'pin:' || fp.user_id and r.kind = 'doubt'),
        'myReaction', (select kind from public.fire_reactions where party_id = p_party and user_id = v_me and week = v_week and day = v_day
                       and target = 'pin:' || fp.user_id and kind <> 'none')) order by fp.at), '[]'::jsonb)
      into v_readings
    from public.fire_pins fp join public.party_members m on m.party_id = fp.party_id and m.user_id = fp.user_id
    where fp.party_id = p_party and fp.week = v_week and fp.day = v_day;
  end if;
  select count(distinct reading) into v_kinds from public.fire_pins where party_id = p_party and week = v_week and day = v_day;

  -- Last night: the previous weekday's call
  if v_day > 1 then v_prev_w := v_week; v_prev_d := v_day - 1;
  elsif v_week > 1 then v_prev_w := v_week - 1; v_prev_d := 6;
  end if;

  return jsonb_build_object('week', v_week, 'day', v_day, 'narrated', v_narrated,
    'evening', (select extract(hour from now() at time zone time_zone) >= 20 from public.parties where id = p_party),
    'pieces', v_pieces,
    'hands', v_hands,
    'clicks', (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object('text', (v_data -> 'clicks' -> (k.idx - 1)) ->> 'text',
                 'names', to_jsonb(k.names), 'solves', coalesce(((v_data -> 'clicks' -> (k.idx - 1)) ->> 'solves')::boolean, false)) order by k.at), '[]'::jsonb)
               from public.fire_clicks k where k.party_id = p_party and k.week = v_week and k.day = v_day),
    'puzzle', v_data -> 'puzzle',
    'thread', case when v_narrated then '[]'::jsonb else (
      select coalesce(jsonb_agg(t.item order by t.at), '[]'::jsonb) from (
        select x.at, x.item from (
          select th.at, jsonb_build_object('kind', th.kind, 'name', m.character_name, 'mine', th.user_id = v_me, 'body', th.body, 'at', th.at) item
          from public.fire_thread th left join public.party_members m on m.party_id = th.party_id and m.user_id = th.user_id
          where th.party_id = p_party and th.week = v_week and th.day = v_day
          union all
          select f.at, jsonb_build_object('kind', 'laid', 'name', m.character_name, 'mine', f.user_id = v_me, 'body', l ->> 'clueTitle', 'at', f.at)
          from public.fan_outs f join public.party_members m on m.party_id = f.party_id and m.user_id = f.user_id
          join lateral jsonb_array_elements(v_data -> 'leads') l on l ->> 'id' = f.lead_id
          where f.party_id = p_party and f.week = v_week and f.day = v_day
          union all
          select s.at, jsonb_build_object('kind', 'laid', 'name', m.character_name, 'mine', s.user_id = v_me, 'body', 'What ' || m.character_name || ' noticed', 'at', s.at)
          from public.fire_shares s join public.party_members m on m.party_id = s.party_id and m.user_id = s.user_id
          where s.party_id = p_party and s.week = v_week and s.day = v_day
          union all
          select l.at, jsonb_build_object('kind', 'laid', 'name', m.character_name, 'mine', l.user_id = v_me,
                   'body', case l.kind when 'pass' then 'What the passers heard' else coalesce(public.fire_press_piece(p_party, v_week, v_day) ->> 'title', 'A find') end, 'at', l.at)
          from public.fire_laid l join public.party_members m on m.party_id = l.party_id and m.user_id = l.user_id
          where l.party_id = p_party and l.week = v_week and l.day = v_day
        ) x order by x.at desc limit 200) t) end,
    'pinned', (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(m.character_name order by fp.at), '[]'::jsonb) from public.fire_pins fp
               join public.party_members m on m.party_id = fp.party_id and m.user_id = fp.user_id
               where fp.party_id = p_party and fp.week = v_week and fp.day = v_day and not v_narrated),
    'readings', v_readings,
    'leaning', case when v_narrated then null when v_kinds > 1 then 'split'
                    when v_kinds = 1 and v_mine_pin.user_id is not null
                         and (select count(*) from public.fire_pins where party_id = p_party and week = v_week and day = v_day) >= 2 then 'same' end,
    'lastCall', case when v_prev_w is not null then public.fire_call(p_party, v_prev_w, v_prev_d) end);
end;
$$;

-- 3. casebook: include unsolvedClick for each night with an unsolved puzzle
create or replace function public.casebook(p_party uuid, p_week int) returns jsonb
language plpgsql security definer set search_path = '' as $$
declare v_week int; v_day int; v_last int; v_out jsonb := '[]'::jsonb; d int; v_data jsonb;
begin
  select o_week, o_day into v_week, v_day from public.my_today_row(p_party);
  if p_week = 0 then p_week := v_week; end if;
  if p_week < 1 or p_week > v_week then raise exception 'not yet'; end if;
  v_last := case when p_week < v_week then 6 else least(v_day, 6) end;
  if p_week = v_week and not exists (select 1 from public.member_days where party_id = p_party and user_id = auth.uid()
                                     and week = v_week and day = v_day and finished_at is not null) then
    v_last := least(v_day - 1, 6);
  end if;
  for d in 1 .. v_last loop
    v_data := public.campfire_data(p_party, p_week, d);
    continue when v_data is null or coalesce((v_data ->> 'narrated')::boolean, false);
    v_out := v_out || jsonb_build_object(
      'day', d,
      'place', v_data ->> 'place',
      'forkA', v_data ->> 'forkA',
      'forkB', v_data ->> 'forkB',
      'pieces', (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object('title', p ->> 'title',
                   'names', (select jsonb_agg(b ->> 'name') from jsonb_array_elements(p -> 'by') b))), '[]'::jsonb)
                 from jsonb_array_elements(public.fire_pieces(p_party, p_week, d)) p),
      'clicks', (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object('text', (v_data -> 'clicks' -> (k.idx - 1)) ->> 'text', 'names', to_jsonb(k.names)) order by k.at), '[]'::jsonb)
                 from public.fire_clicks k where k.party_id = p_party and k.week = p_week and k.day = d),
      'puzzle', v_data -> 'puzzle',
      'call', public.fire_call(p_party, p_week, d),
      'unsolvedClick', case when v_data -> 'puzzle' is not null and not exists (
         select 1 from public.fire_clicks fc where fc.party_id = p_party and fc.week = p_week and fc.day = d
       ) then (select c ->> 'text' from jsonb_array_elements(v_data -> 'clicks') c where coalesce((c ->> 'solves')::boolean, false) limit 1) end
    );
  end loop;
  return jsonb_build_object('week', p_week, 'currentWeek', v_week, 'weekQuestion', (public.campfire_data(p_party, p_week, 1) ->> 'weekQuestion'), 'nights', v_out);
end;
$$;

-- 4. Read-back RPCs:
-- party_read_backs(p_party, p_week, p_day) for weekday chapter reader
create or replace function public.party_read_backs(p_party uuid, p_week int, p_day int) returns jsonb
language plpgsql security definer set search_path = '' as $$
declare
  v_out jsonb := '[]'::jsonb;
  v_my_d1 text;
  v_d3 jsonb;
  v_d2 jsonb;
  v_text text;
begin
  if p_week = 1 and p_day = 2 then
    -- Day 1 was solitary. Read back caller's own call.
    select reading into v_my_d1 from public.fire_pins
    where party_id = p_party and user_id = auth.uid() and week = 1 and day = 1;
    if v_my_d1 = 'A' then
      v_text := 'Last night you called it: He was sent to put it in your hands.';
    elsif v_my_d1 = 'B' then
      v_text := 'Last night you called it: You took it off a man who was carrying it somewhere else.';
    else
      v_text := 'Last night you called it: You took it off a man who was carrying it somewhere else.';
    end if;
    v_out := jsonb_build_array(jsonb_build_object(
      'anchor', 'So the list is hers.',
      'day', 1,
      'text', v_text
    ));
  elsif p_week = 1 and p_day = 4 then
    -- Day 3 read back at Day 4 Pull ("He has half a day on you")
    v_d3 := public.fire_call(p_party, 1, 3);
    if v_d3 ->> 'reading' = 'A' then
      v_text := 'The fire''s call on Day 3: Fenmark is his. He ran back to it.';
    elsif v_d3 ->> 'reading' = 'B' then
      v_text := 'The fire''s call on Day 3: Fenmark is on his way. He was not staying.';
    elsif coalesce((v_d3 ->> 'split')::boolean, false) then
      v_text := 'The fire was split on Day 3.';
    else
      v_text := 'The fire called it on Day 3: Fenmark is his. He ran back to it.';
    end if;
    v_out := jsonb_build_array(jsonb_build_object(
      'anchor', 'He has half a day on you',
      'day', 3,
      'text', v_text
    ));
  elsif p_week = 1 and p_day = 5 then
    -- Day 2 read back at Day 5 ("About the last one.")
    v_d2 := public.fire_call(p_party, 1, 2);
    if v_d2 ->> 'reading' = 'A' then
      v_text := 'The fire''s call on Day 2: Lately. Whatever was happening there is happening now.';
    elsif v_d2 ->> 'reading' = 'B' then
      v_text := 'The fire''s call on Day 2: Long ago. She was writing about an older taking.';
    elsif coalesce((v_d2 ->> 'split')::boolean, false) then
      v_text := 'The fire was split on Day 2.';
    else
      v_text := 'The fire called it on Day 2: Long ago. She was writing about an older taking.';
    end if;
    v_out := jsonb_build_array(jsonb_build_object(
      'anchor', 'About the last one.',
      'day', 2,
      'text', v_text
    ));
  end if;
  return v_out;
end;
$$;

-- gathering_read_backs(p_party, p_week) for live Gathering reader
create or replace function public.gathering_read_backs(p_party uuid, p_week int) returns jsonb
language plpgsql security definer set search_path = '' as $$
declare
  v_out jsonb := '[]'::jsonb;
  v_d4 jsonb;
  v_d5 jsonb;
  v_d6 jsonb;
  v_t4 text;
  v_t5 text;
  v_t6 text;
begin
  if p_week = 1 then
    v_d4 := public.fire_call(p_party, 1, 4);
    if v_d4 ->> 'reading' = 'A' then
      v_t4 := 'The fire called it on Day 4: She was someone in particular. They came for her.';
    elsif v_d4 ->> 'reading' = 'B' then
      v_t4 := 'The fire called it on Day 4: She was the easiest to take.';
    elsif coalesce((v_d4 ->> 'split')::boolean, false) then
      v_t4 := 'The fire was split on Day 4.';
    else
      v_t4 := 'The fire called it on Day 4: She was someone in particular. They came for her.';
    end if;

    v_d5 := public.fire_call(p_party, 1, 5);
    if v_d5 ->> 'reading' = 'A' then
      v_t5 := 'The fire called it on Day 5: It''s the same man, twice.';
    elsif v_d5 ->> 'reading' = 'B' then
      v_t5 := 'The fire called it on Day 5: It''s a way of working, not one man.';
    elsif coalesce((v_d5 ->> 'split')::boolean, false) then
      v_t5 := 'The fire was split on Day 5.';
    else
      v_t5 := 'The fire called it on Day 5: It''s a way of working, not one man.';
    end if;

    v_d6 := public.fire_call(p_party, 1, 6);
    if v_d6 ->> 'reading' = 'A' then
      v_t6 := 'The fire''s case, after Week 1: We are like the children. They want us too.';
    elsif v_d6 ->> 'reading' = 'B' then
      v_t6 := 'The fire''s case, after Week 1: Meira chose us, to help her find them.';
    elsif coalesce((v_d6 ->> 'split')::boolean, false) then
      v_t6 := 'The fire was split on Day 6.';
    else
      v_t6 := 'The fire''s case, after Week 1: Meira chose us, to help her find them.';
    end if;

    v_out := jsonb_build_array(
      jsonb_build_object('anchor', 'The first is Tamsin''s.', 'day', 4, 'text', v_t4),
      jsonb_build_object('anchor', 'Whoever tied them has tied a great many.', 'day', 5, 'text', v_t5),
      jsonb_build_object('anchor', 'None of them is yours.', 'day', 6, 'text', v_t6)
    );
  end if;
  return v_out;
end;
$$;

-- 5. today(p_party): include readBacks
create or replace function public.today(p_party uuid) returns jsonb
language plpgsql security definer set search_path = '' as $$
declare
  v_week int;
  v_day int;
  v_series text;
  v_season int;
  r jsonb;
  v_recaps jsonb;
  v_missed int;
  v_yesterday jsonb;
begin
  select o_week, o_day into v_week, v_day from public.my_today_row(p_party);
  perform public.lock_today_seen_snapshot(p_party, auth.uid());
  update public.member_days set opened_at = coalesce(opened_at, now())
  where party_id = p_party and user_id = auth.uid() and week = v_week and day = v_day;
  perform public.garrick_morning(p_party);
  select o_recaps, o_missed into v_recaps, v_missed from public.my_recaps(p_party);
  if v_week = 1 and v_day = 1 then v_recaps := '[]'::jsonb; v_missed := 0; end if;
  v_yesterday := public.party_yesterday(p_party);
  select series_id, season_number into v_series, v_season from public.parties where id = p_party;
  select jsonb_build_object(
    'week', v_week, 'day', v_day,
    'chapter', (select jsonb_build_object('script', c.script, 'meta', c.meta) from public.chapters c
                where c.series_id = v_series and c.season_number = v_season and c.week = v_week and c.day = v_day),
    'progress', (select to_jsonb(mp) - 'party_id' - 'user_id' from public.member_progress mp where mp.party_id = p_party and mp.user_id = auth.uid()),
    'mine', (select to_jsonb(md) - 'party_id' - 'user_id' from public.member_days md
             where md.party_id = p_party and md.user_id = auth.uid() and md.week = v_week and md.day = v_day),
    'claims', public.party_claims(p_party),
    'daysPlayed', (select count(*) from public.member_days md where md.party_id = p_party and md.user_id = auth.uid() and md.finished_at is not null),
    'recaps', v_recaps,
    'missed', v_missed,
    'partyYesterday', v_yesterday,
    'readBacks', public.party_read_backs(p_party, v_week, v_day)
  ) into r;
  return r;
end;
$$;

-- 6. g_view(p_party, p_week, p_user): include readBacks
create or replace function public.g_view(p_party uuid, p_week int, p_user uuid) returns jsonb
language plpgsql stable security definer set search_path = '' as $$
declare g public.gatherings; d jsonb; s jsonb; steps jsonb; meta jsonb; e jsonb; st jsonb; out jsonb := '[]'::jsonb; item jsonb;
        here uuid[]; v_k text; v_attr text; v_fell boolean; v_series text; v_season int; v_rows jsonb; v_res int; v_me text := p_user::text;
        v_earn jsonb; v_lines jsonb; v_line text; v_gold int; v_parts text[]; v_tz text; v_ue_won boolean; v_asked int;
begin
  select * into g from public.gatherings where party_id = p_party and week = p_week;
  d := public.g_script(p_party, p_week); steps := d -> 'steps'; meta := d -> 'meta'; s := g.state;
  here := public.g_here(p_party, p_week);
  select series_id, season_number, time_zone into v_series, v_season, v_tz from public.parties where id = p_party;
  v_fell := exists (select 1 from jsonb_array_elements(s -> 'battle' -> 'fighters') x where x ->> 'id' = v_me and (x ->> 'fallen')::boolean);
  v_ue_won := s -> 'ue' ->> 'outcome' = 'won';

  for e in select x from jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(s -> 'log', '[]'::jsonb)) x loop
    st := steps -> (e ->> 'i')::int; v_k := e ->> 'i'; item := e;
    case e ->> 't'
      when 'act' then
        item := item || jsonb_build_object('by', s -> 'tappedBy' -> v_k, 'tapped', s -> 'tapped' ? v_k);
      when 'notice' then
        if v_fell and st -> 'lines' ? 'floor' then
          item := item || jsonb_build_object('attr', 'floor', 'text', public.g_fill(p_party, st -> 'lines' ->> 'floor', s));
        else
          v_attr := public.g_top_attr(p_party, p_user, st -> 'lines');
          item := item || jsonb_build_object('attr', v_attr, 'text', public.g_fill(p_party, st -> 'lines' ->> v_attr, s));
        end if;
      when 'lookCloser' then
        v_attr := public.g_top_attr(p_party, p_user, st -> 'lines');
        item := item || jsonb_build_object('attr', v_attr,
          'offered', not v_fell and not (p_week = 5 and s -> 'ue' ->> 'outcome' = 'lost') and s -> 'order' ? v_me,
          'mine', s -> 'look' -> v_me,
          'line', case when (s -> 'look' -> v_me ->> 'pass')::boolean then public.g_fill(p_party, st -> 'lines' ->> (s -> 'look' -> v_me ->> 'attr'), s) end,
          'score', public.g_score(p_party, p_user, v_attr), 'dc', (meta ->> 'dc')::int);
      when 'pick' then
        v_res := (s -> 'result' ->> v_k)::int;
        item := item || jsonb_build_object('mode', st ->> 'mode', 'question', st ->> 'question', 'options', st -> 'options',
          'mine', s -> 'picks' -> v_k -> v_me, 'result', v_res, 'count', (select count(*) from jsonb_object_keys(coalesce(s -> 'picks' -> v_k, '{}'::jsonb))),
          'chosen', case when st ->> 'mode' = 'chosen' then public.g_name(p_party, (s ->> 'chosen')::uuid) end,
          'chosenIsMe', st ->> 'mode' = 'chosen' and s ->> 'chosen' = v_me,
          'chooseFrom', case when st ->> 'mode' = 'chosen' then (e ->> 'at')::timestamptz + interval '30 seconds' end,
          'votes', case when st ->> 'mode' = 'vote' or v_res is not null then
            (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object('name', public.g_name(p_party, key::uuid), 'o', value::int)), '[]'::jsonb)
             from jsonb_each_text(coalesce(s -> 'picks' -> v_k, '{}'::jsonb))) end);
      when 'clue' then
        item := item || jsonb_build_object('title', st ->> 'title', 'text', public.g_fill(p_party, st ->> 'text', s));
      when 'ueRoll' then
        item := item || jsonb_build_object('attr', s -> 'ue' ->> 'attr',
          'rolls', (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object(
            'id', key, 'name', public.g_name(p_party, key::uuid),
            'd20', (value ->> 'd20')::int, 'score', (value ->> 'score')::int, 'bonus', (value ->> 'bonus')::int,
            'map', (value ->> 'map')::int, 'relic', (value ->> 'relic')::int, 'dc', (value ->> 'dc')::int,
            'net', (value ->> 'net')::int, 'pass', (value ->> 'pass')::boolean) order by (value ->> 'at')), '[]'::jsonb)
            from jsonb_each(coalesce(s -> 'ue' -> 'rolls', '{}'::jsonb))));
      when 'summary' then
        v_earn := public.g_earn(p_party, p_week, p_user);
        v_gold := (v_earn ->> 'gold')::int;
        v_asked := (select count(*) from jsonb_object_keys(coalesce(s -> 'asks', '{}'::jsonb)));
        v_parts := array[]::text[];
        if (s -> 'battle' ->> 'won')::boolean then v_parts := array_append(v_parts, 'Battle won');
        else v_parts := array_append(v_parts, 'Battle: broke through'); end if;
        if v_ue_won then v_parts := array_append(v_parts, st ->> 'ueWon');
        else v_parts := array_append(v_parts, st ->> 'ueLost'); end if;
        v_parts := array_append(v_parts, v_asked || ' ' || case when v_asked = 1 then 'question' else 'questions' end || ' asked');
        v_lines := '[]'::jsonb;
        for v_line in select jsonb_array_elements_text(st -> 'lines') loop
          v_line := replace(v_line, '{EARNED}', '+' || v_gold || 'g, +1 level to every Attribute, +1 Relic');
          v_line := replace(v_line, '{PARTY_SUMMARY}', array_to_string(v_parts, ' · '));
          v_line := replace(v_line, '{asked}', v_asked::text);
          v_line := replace(v_line, '{battle}', case when (s -> 'battle' ->> 'won')::boolean then 'won' else 'broke through' end);
          if st -> 'ue' ? 'success' and st -> 'ue' ? 'fail' then
            v_line := replace(v_line, '{ue:' || (st -> 'ue' ->> 'success') || '|' || (st -> 'ue' ->> 'fail') || '}',
                              case when v_ue_won then st -> 'ue' ->> 'success' else st -> 'ue' ->> 'fail' end);
          end if;
          v_lines := v_lines || to_jsonb(v_line);
        end loop;
        item := item || jsonb_build_object('lines', v_lines, 'earn', v_earn);
      else
        null;
    end case;
    out := out || jsonb_build_array(item);
  end loop;

  return jsonb_build_object(
    'week', p_week, 'version', g.version, 'now', now(),
    'opensAt', g.opens_at, 'startedAt', g.started_at, 'endedAt', g.ended_at,
    'cursor', g.cursor, 'waitUntil', g.wait_until,
    'timeZone', v_tz, 'tonight', d ->> 'tonight',
    'ueAttr', meta ->> 'ueAttr',
    'party', (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object('id', m.user_id, 'name', m.character_name,
                                 'here', m.user_id = any(here), 'in', m.user_id = any(g.in_party)) order by m.joined_at), '[]'::jsonb)
              from public.party_members m where m.party_id = p_party and m.approved_at is not null),
    'me', p_user, 'isHost', public.is_party_host(p_party, p_user),
    'n', case when g.started_at is not null then coalesce(array_length(g.in_party, 1), 0) end,
    'log', out,
    'weeksBest', public.gathering_weeks_best(p_party, p_week),
    'readBacks', public.gathering_read_backs(p_party, p_week),
    'seasonTitles', case when p_week = 6 and g.ended_at is not null then public.party_season_titles(p_party) end,
    'progress', (select jsonb_build_object('gold', mp.gold, 'attrs', mp.attrs, 'relics', mp.relics,
                   'weapon', mp.weapon_level, 'armor', mp.armor_level)
                 from public.member_progress mp where mp.party_id = p_party and mp.user_id = p_user),
    'battle', case when (meta ->> 'battle')::boolean then
      jsonb_build_object('enemy', meta -> 'enemy', 'rounds', s -> 'battle' -> 'rounds' -> v_me,
        'fighter', (select x from jsonb_array_elements(s -> 'battle' -> 'fighters') x where x ->> 'id' = v_me),
        'otherFighters', (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object('name', x ->> 'name', 'hp', (x ->> 'hp')::int, 'fallen', (x ->> 'fallen')::boolean)), '[]'::jsonb)
                          from jsonb_array_elements(s -> 'battle' -> 'fighters') x where x ->> 'id' <> v_me)) end,
    'lore', case when (meta ->> 'lore')::boolean then
      jsonb_build_object('scripture', meta -> 'scripture', 'matchOptions', meta -> 'matchOptions',
        'myMatch', s -> 'matches' -> v_me, 'matchResult', s -> 'matchResult', 'matchOrder', s -> 'matchOrder') end,
    'ask', case when (meta ->> 'ask')::boolean then
      jsonb_build_object('rows', (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object(
        'group', r ->> 'group',
        'questions', (select jsonb_agg(case when not (r ->> 'sealed')::boolean or s ? 'unsealed' then q else '???' end)
                      from jsonb_array_elements_text(r -> 'questions') q),
        'askedBy', (select public.g_name(p_party, key::uuid) from jsonb_each_text(coalesce(s -> 'asks', '{}'::jsonb))
                    where value = (r -> 'questions' ->> 0) limit 1),
        'answer', case when exists (select 1 from jsonb_each_text(coalesce(s -> 'asks', '{}'::jsonb))
                                    where value = (r -> 'questions' ->> 0)) then r ->> 'answer' end)), '[]'::jsonb)
        from jsonb_array_elements(d -> 'askRows') r),
        'order', (select coalesce(jsonb_agg(public.g_name(p_party, u::uuid)), '[]'::jsonb)
                  from jsonb_array_elements_text(coalesce(s -> 'askOrder', '[]'::jsonb)) u),
        'turn', case when s ->> 'askTurn' is not null then public.g_name(p_party, (s ->> 'askTurn')::uuid) end,
        'turnIsMe', s ->> 'askTurn' = v_me,
        'myAsk', s -> 'asks' -> v_me,
        'askedCount', (select count(*) from jsonb_object_keys(coalesce(s -> 'asks', '{}'::jsonb))),
        'totalToAsk', coalesce(array_length(g.in_party, 1), 0)) end
  );
end;
$$;

revoke execute on function public.party_read_backs(uuid, int, int), public.gathering_read_backs(uuid, int) from public, anon, authenticated;
grant execute on function public.party_read_backs(uuid, int, int), public.gathering_read_backs(uuid, int) to authenticated;
